# Breeches, Eager Pillager: "Whenever a Pirate you control attacks" - an opponent's Pirate attacking does not trigger it (CR 603.2c), and "that hasn't been chosen this turn" counts only the current turn
# (CR 700.2), so Breeches may choose the same mode on a later turn. Bot1 casts Breeches on turn 1 and attacks with it on turn 3, choosing the Treasure. On turn 4 Bot2's Goblin Tomb Raider (a Pirate,
# hasty under its Mox) attacks Bot1: Breeches is not triggered and Bot1 has no more than its one Treasure. On turn 5 Breeches attacks again and chooses the Treasure again: two Treasures.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Breeches, Eager Pillager
Plains x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Goblin Tomb Raider
Island x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Breeches, Eager Pillager.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot2.Hand.Goblin Tomb Raider.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Breeches, Eager Pillager > Bot2)
Bot1.Modes(Create a Treasure)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Treasure Token.Types = Artifact
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Attack(Goblin Tomb Raider > Bot1)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]
? Stack.Count = 0
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 2
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Breeches, Eager Pillager > Bot2)
Bot1.Modes(Create a Treasure)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 3
Bot1.Life = 18
Bot2.Life = 14
